&lt;p&gt;digiLab is a formative AI company with world-leading specialists in uncertainty quantification, applied where the stakes are highest and the margin for error is smallest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers are among the largest and most advanced engineering and science-led organisations in the world, and they&#39;re using our technology to tackle some of society&#39;s biggest challenges. How do we make fusion energy a commercial reality? Can we drive down the cost of renewable energy and accelerate the transition to a sustainable future? How do we support coral reef restoration, or strengthen Britain&#39;s national security? These are just a few of the critical questions our technology is helping to answer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the heart of our work is digiLab&#39;s trustworthy and explainable AI platform, enabling our customers to accelerate innovation, reduce risk, and deliver real value through better informed decisions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for ambitious team members to help shape our pioneering technology and tackle some of the world&#39;s most impactful problems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This full-time position (Monday to Thursday), reporting to the Chief Marketing &amp;amp; Strategy Officer, leads the development and delivery of digiLab’s marketing programmes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on leadership role. You will help shape our positioning, develop campaigns, launch products and build the processes that make marketing effective as the company scales. You should be comfortable moving between strategic decisions and practical execution, from planning a market campaign to editing a customer story or improving a sales presentation. Your challenge will be to make sophisticated technology understandable and commercially relevant to engineering leaders, enterprise buyers and technology partners. You will work directly with technical and commercial leaders, with meaningful ownership of the marketing programme and its impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Marketing Director at digiLab, you will be responsible for:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building integrated campaigns that generate qualified opportunities and support expansion within existing accounts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with commercial leads on target-account programmes, events, webinars and prospect engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Planning product launches and creating sales materials that explain what customers can buy, how it works and why it matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establishing shared definitions and reporting for marketing contribution to pipeline, conversion and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with the research and product teams to translate technical work into compelling content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing customer stories that connect technical outcomes with business value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building digiLab’s presence through relevant industry events and expert communities, maintaining accuracy in technical and commercial claims.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing joint campaigns, content and events with engineering and technology partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Giving partners the messaging and materials they need to introduce digiLab to their customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the marketing calendar, budget and delivery process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing agencies, freelancers and specialist suppliers, and helping build the internal team as requirements grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving the website, CRM integration, campaign measurement and content production process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritising the activities that deliver results within a startup’s resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Duties may evolve, and you may be asked to take on other reasonable responsibilities within your competence to support our growth.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading B2B marketing for enterprise software, AI, deep technology or a closely related business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A record of translating complex products into clear propositions and effective campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting enterprise sales cycles and working closely with commercial teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical knowledge of demand generation, digital channels, marketing measurement and HubSpot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to work credibly with technical specialists and draw out what matters to customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing budgets and external resources, with a willingness to do the work yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgement about priorities, a collaborative approach and comfort operating with incomplete information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On-site at either our Exeter or Bristol office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;As an ambitious, rapidly-growing start-up, we’re looking for proactive, adaptable people who thrive in a fast-paced environment. Our standard working hours are 9.00–5.30pm, Monday to Thursday, though some flexibility outside these hours may be required to meet business needs.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Culture and Values&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At digiLab, we&#39;re building something we truly believe in, and we&#39;re looking for like-minded people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;We foster a culture of innovation, trust, and collaboration. Our values include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Creativity &amp;amp; Agility:&lt;/strong&gt; Encouraging innovation and flexibility in goal achievement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trust &amp;amp; Responsibility:&lt;/strong&gt; Supporting each other in taking calculated risks for bold innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Open &amp;amp; Honest Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensuring transparent communication and alignment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High-Performance Standards:&lt;/strong&gt; Continuously challenging ourselves to excel in delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Value-Driven Work:&lt;/strong&gt; Regularly assessing our contributions toward company goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We value enthusiasm and loyalty, and we’re committed to offering a great work-life balance. Along with the exciting challenges this role provides, we offer a range of benefits including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive Salary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Personal &amp;amp; professional development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BUPA private health care (via salary sacrifice)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Cashplan&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cycle to work scheme&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Referral Program&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regular social events such as pizza nights, kayaking, bouldering and bake offs&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;digiLab is an equal opportunity employer. We welcome applications from candidates of all backgrounds and are committed to ensuring our recruitment processes are fair, inclusive, and legally compliant. We take equality, dignity, and non-discrimination seriously.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Final Note:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We aim to respond to every applicant, but due to high application volumes, we may not be able to respond individually. Thank you for your interest in joining the digiLab team. The information you provide will be stored and used in line with our Privacy Notice.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;London, Warwick, Manchester,&amp;nbsp;Derby&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At BakerHicks, ​​​​​​​our Electrical Services team works with clients across multiple sectors, delivering large and complex projects which require highly resilient power supplies. Specialising in heavily-regulated industries where quality and safety are key, we’re experienced in all aspects of the project lifecycle from definition and feasibility to detailed design and site monitoring.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are actively recruiting across this capability to support a growing portfolio of live projects and welcome applications from Senior and Principal-level contractors to join the team to support the workload.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Electrical Services teams work across a range of UK projects, delivering complex solutions within Nuclear, Defence and other regulated sectors, alongside wider infrastructure and energy environments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Roles are available across multiple locations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Deliver engineering design and consultancy services for BakerHicks under the direction of the line manager or project lead.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Produce design outputs (drawings, specifications, reports), undertake site surveys, support construction stages, liaise with clients and design/construction teams, manage projects, oversee costing, and ensure progress against the project brief.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Check calculations and detailed drawings to ensure designs meet quality standards, compliance requirements, and client expectations.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Work collaboratively with multi‑disciplinary teams to deliver safe, efficient, and buildable solutions.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Maintain an understanding of CDM requirements.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Projects range from early design through to delivery and operational support, providing exposure to technically challenging and safety‑critical environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;9o5f4y&quot; data-start=&quot;95&quot; data-end=&quot;226&quot;&gt;Confidence in producing high-quality designs, with the technical capability to carry out independent checks and ensure accuracy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;1iqopol&quot; data-start=&quot;227&quot; data-end=&quot;377&quot;&gt;A strong awareness of commercial considerations, with the ability to identify and flag potential risks or concerns where appropriate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-section-id=&quot;ksehg&quot; data-start=&quot;378&quot; data-end=&quot;565&quot;&gt;A solid understanding of project delivery and people management principles, enabling effective anticipation of challenges and proactive escalation of risks or recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
