&lt;p&gt;The Director of Channel Sales is responsible for leading a team of Channel Sales representatives to drive sales efforts to meet and exceed Net New Annual Recurring Revenue (ARR) targets from a specified Area. This is an extremely hands-on role that will actively manage their teams who are responsible for building partnerships and growing Net New business through strong partnerships within a specified Area. The Director will align with the strategy for Channel Sales growth to execute strategic plans, grow pipeline and achieve revenue goals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Manage a team of Channel Sales representatives to execute revenue strategies, and exceed KPIs and ARR targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the day-to-day activities of Channel Sales reps through daily team standups, close analysis of sales statistics and pipeline reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with partners directly to build strategic relationships and growth of key partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist Channel Sales reps in building partner sales engagements and closing deals with partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Develop, drive and guide our partner activities to foster excellent relationships with new and existing partners aligned to the partner stratification to grow net new revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Conduct weekly rhythm of the business reviews with VP and other sales enablement teams to identify trends and provide feedback on areas of opportunity and improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Validate sales representative staging and Area pipeline health to ensure accurate forecasting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Collaborate with senior leadership and SMB, Mid-Market and Enterprise leaders to align the business and drive growth through partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Collaborate with Area Customer Success Leader to ensure the teams are aligned with all sales strategies and goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Conduct interviews with potential sales candidates to build a world class sales team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Manage Area sales budget requests for events, trade shows, ect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Minimum 6-8 years Channel sales experience required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Minimum 5 years of people management experience in the assigned area required of 8 or more employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience in IT Channel Sales (SaaS preferred)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Bachelor degree or equivalent higher education experience,&amp;nbsp;desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience collaborating with Partner businesses and leading&amp;nbsp;Channel sales teams, desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with standard concepts and practices within the IT,&amp;nbsp;Security, Cloud Email Security or Cybersecurity industry, desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience with Salesforce, a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience with Gmail and Google Docs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience with MS Office (Word and Excel)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Experience with web browsers (Chrome, Internet Explorer, ect&lt;/li&gt;
